+- **Performance:** Efficient on GPU due to parallelizable element-wise assignment [S1, S2, unofficial].
+- **Strengths:** Simple, fast, and reduces memory footprint by 33% for symmetric matrices [S1, S2, S3, unofficial].
+- **Limitations:** Only applicable to symmetric matrices; does not handle non-symmetric inputs gracefully [S1, S2, S3, unofficial].
 
 ## Background
-Symmetric Matrix Stripping is used in 3D Gaussian Splatting implementations to manage covariance matrices efficiently. It appears in projects such as InstantSplat and 4D Gaussian Splatting, where it facilitates the handling of Gaussian parameters during training and rendering [S1, S2, unofficial].
+Symmetric Matrix Stripping is used in 3D Gaussian Splatting and related rendering techniques to efficiently handle covariance matrices for Gaussian primitives [S1, S2, S3, unofficial]. It was popularized in implementations such as InstantSplat [S1, unofficial], FastGS [S2, unofficial], and 4D-Gaussian-Splatting [S3, unofficial] for optimizing the storage and processing of 3D Gaussians.
 
